: "loop", "pos": "v./n.", "zh": "循环；兜圈子", "ex": "To loop means to go around and around and repeat. Keep looping on the same game means playing the same game again and again without moving on. It's also used for songs and videos that repeat.", "exs": ["This song has been looping in my head all day.", "Set the video to loop."], "t": 127.71, "tt": {"w": 127.71, "ex": [["To", 130.18], ["loop", 130.37], ["means", 130.37], ["to", 130.41], ["go", 130.67], ["around", 130.83], ["and", 131.17], ["around", 131.53], ["and", 131.77], ["repeat.", 132.21], ["Keep", 133.31], ["looping", 133.51], ["on", 134.03], ["the", 134.21], ["same", 134.33], ["game", 134.55], ["means", 134.93], ["playing", 135.37], ["the", 135.77], ["same", 136.01], ["game", 136.25], ["again", 136.79], ["and", 137.07], ["again", 137.27], ["without", 137.57], ["moving", 138.13], ["on.", 138.61], ["It's", 139.53], ["also", 139.77], ["used", 140.11], ["for", 140.39], ["songs", 140.67], ["and", 140.93], ["videos", 141.37], ["that", 141.71], ["repeat.", 142.03]], "exs": [[["This", 145.66], ["song", 145.71], ["has", 145.87], ["been", 146.11], ["looping", 146.31], ["in", 146.75], ["my", 146.85], ["head", 146.97], ["all", 147.23], ["day.", 147.51]], [["Set", 152.71], ["the", 152.76], ["video", 152.83], ["to", 153.07], ["loop.", 153.33]]], "z": [148.53, 154.31], "o": 157.37}, "src": {"t": "You don’t wanna just keep looping on the same game over and over,", "a": "audio/t03/s05.mp3", "hl": [26, 33], "sp": "Naval", "oa": "audio/t03o/s05.mp3", "oab": [0.82, 2.83], "oas": ["audio/t03o/s05.mp3", "audio/t03o/s06.mp3"]}}, {"n": 6, "w": "although", "pos": "conj.", "zh": "虽然；尽管", "ex": "Although connects two ideas that seem to go against each other. Naval says don't keep looping, although these games are very enticing. It means the same as even though, and sounds a bit more formal than but.", "exs": ["Although I was tired, I went to the gym.", "I liked the movie, although it was a little long."], "t": 160.77, "tt": {"w": 160.77, 